IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tda-common`

-- Duties Act 2001 (Tas) Chapter 8 -- duty on registering a motor vehicle. SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE, in the Act's terms ("the
-- applicant for registration", "the person acquiring the beneficial ownership", "the Commissioner"); the questions are
-- in tda-seat.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 192 (what is charged), s 193(1) (statement of dutiable value with the application; regulative),
-- s 195 (who pays), s 196 (when duty becomes payable) and s 196A (failure to pay is a tax default; regulative with
-- s 196), s 197 (the rates, from 1 October 2007), s 198 (dutiable value). The s 3 definitions used: "motor vehicle"
-- (Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999: a FACT), "heavy vehicle" (Heavy Vehicle National Law (Tasmania) Act 2013, not a camper
-- van: a FACT), "market value", "passenger vehicle" (s 197(4)-(5), worked out from facts).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the exemptions and refunds in ss 199-203 (an application claiming one answers `not covered`); s 193(2)
-- and ss 203A-218 (dealers' exemption certificates); s 194 (the Commissioner's assessment where no application was
-- made, which follows the same rates).
--
-- Edition: consolidation published 2026-10-13, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2001-015.txt. Based on
-- material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 20 October 2026 (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2001 Chapter 8 -- motor vehicle duty (seat-neutral core)`

§§ `s 192 -- what is charged`

-- s 192: "This Chapter charges duty on -- (a) an application to register a motor vehicle under the Vehicle and Traffic
-- Act 1999 if -- (i) the vehicle has not previously been registered under that Act; or (ii) the person in whose name the
-- vehicle is to be registered differs (or the persons ... differ) from the person or persons in whose name or names the
-- vehicle was last registered; or (b) a notice of a change of beneficial ownership of a motor vehicle given under the
-- Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999."
DECLARE `Vehicle dealing` IS ONE OF
    `an application to register a vehicle not previously registered under the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999`
    `an application to register a vehicle in a name or names different from its last registration`
    `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership`
    `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration`

GIVEN `d` IS A `Vehicle dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is charged with duty (s 192)` IF
    CONSIDER `d`
    WHEN `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 195: "Duty is payable by -- (a) the applicant for registration of the motor vehicle; or (b) in the case of a change
-- in beneficial ownership of a motor vehicle, the person acquiring the beneficial ownership; or (c) [a motor dealer or
-- trader on a reassessment]". The seat is (a) or (b).
DECLARE `Vehicle duty payer` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant for registration (s 195(a))`
    `the person acquiring the beneficial ownership (s 195(b))`
    `no one: the application is not charged (s 192)`

GIVEN `d` IS A `Vehicle dealing`
GIVETH A `Vehicle duty payer`
`who pays the vehicle duty (s 195)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `d`
    WHEN `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership` THEN `the person acquiring the beneficial ownership (s 195(b))`
    WHEN `an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration` THEN `no one: the application is not charged (s 192)`
    OTHERWISE `the applicant for registration (s 195(a))`

§§ `The vehicle and the dealing`

DECLARE `Vehicle facts` HAS
    `the day of the application`                                                             IS A DATE
    `the dealing`                                                                            IS A `Vehicle dealing`
    `is a heavy vehicle (Heavy Vehicle National Law, not a camper van)`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a motor cycle`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `is constructed principally for the carriage of passengers`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `is designed for not more than 9 adults and built on a truck chassis or with off-road features` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a utility or panel van body whose forward part and mechanics are those of the maker's passenger vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is equipped to seat more than 9 adults, including the driver`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a new motor vehicle`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the manufacturer gave the purchaser a discount off the normal retail price not available to the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consideration`                                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the market value`                                                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the consideration is adequate for the value of the new vehicle (s 198(1A))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed`                                            IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 197(4): "A passenger vehicle is a motor vehicle, other than a heavy vehicle or motor cycle, that is -- (a)
-- constructed principally for the carriage of passengers; or (b) designed principally for the conveyance of not more
-- than 9 adult persons, including the driver, and is constructed either on a truck chassis or with special features for
-- off-road operation." (5): "A passenger vehicle does not include a motor vehicle that -- (a) has a utility or panel van
-- type body in which the forward part of the body form and the greater part of the mechanical equipment are the same as
-- those in a passenger vehicle manufactured by the manufacturer of the motor vehicle; or (b) is constructed for the
-- carriage of passengers and equipped to seat more than 9 adult persons, including the driver."
GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a passenger vehicle (s 197(4)-(5))` IF
        (NOT `v`'s `is a heavy vehicle (Heavy Vehicle National Law, not a camper van)`)
    AND (NOT `v`'s `is a motor cycle`)
    AND (    `v`'s `is constructed principally for the carriage of passengers`
         OR `v`'s `is designed for not more than 9 adults and built on a truck chassis or with off-road features`)
    AND (NOT `v`'s `has a utility or panel van body whose forward part and mechanics are those of the maker's passenger vehicle`)
    AND (NOT `v`'s `is equipped to seat more than 9 adults, including the driver`)

-- s 197(6): "A manufacturer's fleet discount in respect of a motor vehicle is a discount -- (a) that is given to the
-- purchaser of the motor vehicle by the manufacturer of the motor vehicle; and (b) that is deducted from the normal
-- retail price of the motor vehicle; and (c) that is not available to the general public."
GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a manufacturer's fleet discount has been provided (s 197(6))` IF
    `v`'s `the manufacturer gave the purchaser a discount off the normal retail price not available to the general public`

§§ `s 198 -- dutiable value`

-- s 198(1): "The dutiable value of a registered motor vehicle is -- (a) the consideration in money or money's worth
-- given for the acquisition of the vehicle; or (b) the market value of the vehicle at the time of acquisition of the
-- vehicle or lodgement of a notice of change of beneficial ownership of the vehicle -- whichever is the greater."
-- (1A): "The dutiable value of a new motor vehicle is the consideration ..., if the Commissioner is satisfied that the
-- consideration is adequate in relation to the value of that motor vehicle." (2): in any other case, the greater of the
-- consideration and "the market value of the vehicle at the time of application to register". (3) leaves out an
-- extended warranty premium, equipment moved from the applicant's other vehicle, and unrelated equipment: the buyer
-- states the consideration without them. The time at which market value is taken is a FACT in the market value given.
GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 198)` MEANS
    IF     `v`'s `is a new motor vehicle`
       AND `v`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied the consideration is adequate for the value of the new vehicle (s 198(1A))`
    THEN `v`'s `the consideration`
    ELSE `the greater of` (`v`'s `the consideration`) (`v`'s `the market value`)

§§ `s 197 -- the rates, from 1 October 2007`

-- s 197(1): "$3 per $100, or part, of the dutiable value of the motor vehicle, except as provided by subsections (2),
-- (3), (3A) and (3B)." (2) passenger vehicles: "(a) if the dutiable value ... does not exceed $35 000, $3 per $100, or
-- part; (b) if [it] exceeds $35 000 but does not exceed $40 000, $1 050 plus $11 for every $100 or part of $100 of the
-- dutiable value ... that exceeds $35 000; (c) if [it] exceeds $40 000, for every $100 or part of $100 of that dutiable
-- value, $4." (3): "The rate of duty applicable to a heavy vehicle the dutiable value of which does not exceed $2 000 or
-- to a motor vehicle the dutiable value of which does not exceed $600 is $20." (3A): "Despite subsection (2), the rate of
-- duty for a new motor vehicle, other than a heavy vehicle, for which a manufacturer's fleet discount has been provided
-- is $3.50 per $100, or part". (3B): "The rate of duty for a heavy vehicle is $1.00 per $100, or part".
-- ORDER (finding 13): (3) is read first, as a fixed duty for low values that (1), (2), (3A) and (3B) do not displace
-- ((3B) alone would give $10 on a $1,000 heavy vehicle); then (3B) for heavy vehicles; then (3A), which applies "despite
-- subsection (2)"; then (2); then (1).
DECLARE `Vehicle rate` IS ONE OF
    `the fixed $20 (s 197(3))`
    `the heavy vehicle rate, $1 per $100 or part (s 197(3B))`
    `the fleet discount rate, $3.50 per $100 or part (s 197(3A))`
    `the passenger vehicle rate (s 197(2))`
    `the general rate, $3 per $100 or part (s 197(1))`

GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle facts`
GIVETH A `Vehicle rate`
`the s 197 rate for` MEANS
    IF     `the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 198)` `v` AT MOST 600
        OR (    `v`'s `is a heavy vehicle (Heavy Vehicle National Law, not a camper van)`
            AND `the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 198)` `v` AT MOST 2000)
    THEN `the fixed $20 (s 197(3))`
    ELSE IF `v`'s `is a heavy vehicle (Heavy Vehicle National Law, not a camper van)`
         THEN `the heavy vehicle rate, $1 per $100 or part (s 197(3B))`
         ELSE IF     `v`'s `is a new motor vehicle`
                 AND `a manufacturer's fleet discount has been provided (s 197(6))` `v`
              THEN `the fleet discount rate, $3.50 per $100 or part (s 197(3A))`
              ELSE IF `is a passenger vehicle (s 197(4)-(5))` `v`
                   THEN `the passenger vehicle rate (s 197(2))`
                   ELSE `the general rate, $3 per $100 or part (s 197(1))`

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the passenger vehicle duty on` MEANS
    IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 35000
    THEN 3 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`
    ELSE IF `the dutiable value` AT MOST 40000
         THEN 1050 PLUS (11 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the dutiable value` MINUS 35000))
         ELSE 4 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`

GIVEN `rate` IS A `Vehicle rate`, `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at` `rate` `on` `the dutiable value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `rate`
    WHEN `the fixed $20 (s 197(3))` THEN 20
    WHEN `the heavy vehicle rate, $1 per $100 or part (s 197(3B))` THEN 1 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`
    WHEN `the fleet discount rate, $3.50 per $100 or part (s 197(3A))` THEN 3.50 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`
    WHEN `the passenger vehicle rate (s 197(2))` THEN `the passenger vehicle duty on` `the dutiable value`
    WHEN `the general rate, $3 per $100 or part (s 197(1))` THEN 3 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`

DECLARE `Vehicle duty answer` IS ONE OF
    `the vehicle duty, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `at` IS A `Vehicle rate`
    `no duty: the application is not charged (s 192)`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `v` IS A `Vehicle facts`
GIVETH A `Vehicle duty answer`
`the vehicle duty on` MEANS
    IF `v`'s `the day of the application` `is before` (YMD 2007 10 1)
    THEN `not covered` `the vehicle application is dated before 1 October 2007, when the s 197 rates were last amended (No. 18 of 2007); the rates in force before then are not in the deposited consolidation`
    ELSE IF (NOT `is charged with duty (s 192)` (`v`'s `the dealing`))
         THEN `no duty: the application is not charged (s 192)`
         ELSE IF `v`'s `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed`
              THEN `not covered` `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed for the vehicle: those exemptions are not encoded`
              ELSE `the vehicle duty, in dollars, is` (`the duty at` (`the s 197 rate for` `v`) `on` (`the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 198)` `v`)) (`the s 197 rate for` `v`)

§§ `ss 193(1), 196, 196A -- the statement with the application, and paying when registered (regulative)`

-- s 193(1): "A person who is required by law to make an application to register a motor vehicle ... or give a notice of
-- a change of beneficial ownership must lodge with the application for registration or the notice a statement of the
-- dutiable value of the vehicle, unless the application or notice is not chargeable with duty under this Chapter.
-- Penalty: Fine not exceeding 100 penalty units." s 196: "Duty becomes payable on -- (a) the date on which -- (i) the
-- motor vehicle is registered or the registration is transferred in pursuance of the relevant application; or (ii) a
-- notice of a change in beneficial ownership is lodged". s 196A: "A failure to pay duty when it becomes payable under
-- section 196 is a tax default for the purposes of the Taxation Administration Act 1997." The clock starts on the day of
-- the application or notice; the statement is due that same day. The duty is due on the day of registration for an
-- application, and on the day the notice is lodged for a notice (s 196(a)(ii)): the caller gives the days to that day,
-- 0 for a notice.
-- Who is bound (s 193(1), s 195): for an application, the applicant both lodges the statement and pays (s 195(a)); for a
-- notice of a change of beneficial ownership, the person giving the notice lodges the statement, and "the person
-- acquiring the beneficial ownership" pays (s 195(b)).
`the same day` MEANS 0

GIVEN `d` IS A `Vehicle dealing`
GIVETH A `Party`
`the party who must lodge the statement (s 193(1))` MEANS
    CONSIDER `d`
    WHEN `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership` THEN `the person giving the notice of a change of beneficial ownership`
    OTHERWISE `the applicant to register the vehicle`

GIVEN `d` IS A `Vehicle dealing`
GIVETH A `Party`
`the party who must pay the vehicle duty (s 195)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `d`
    WHEN `a notice of a change of beneficial ownership` THEN `the person acquiring the beneficial ownership`
    OTHERWISE `the applicant to register the vehicle`

GIVEN `the dealing`                                      IS A `Vehicle dealing`
      `days from the application to the day duty is payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`ss 193(1), 196, 196A -- lodge the value statement with the application or notice and pay when duty is payable` `the dealing` `days from the application to the day duty is payable` MEANS
    IF (NOT `is charged with duty (s 192)` `the dealing`)
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE    (PARTY `the party who must lodge the statement (s 193(1))` `the dealing`
             MUST  `lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application`
             WITHIN `the same day`
             LEST  BREACH BY (`the party who must lodge the statement (s 193(1))` `the dealing`) BECAUSE "s 193(1): a statement of the dutiable value must be lodged with the application for registration or the notice of change of beneficial ownership; fine not exceeding 100 penalty units")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the party who must pay the vehicle duty (s 195)` `the dealing`
             MUST  `pay the duty`
             WITHIN `days from the application to the day duty is payable`
             LEST  BREACH BY (`the party who must pay the vehicle duty (s 195)` `the dealing`) BECAUSE "ss 195, 196, 196A: duty becomes payable on the day the vehicle is registered or the registration transferred, or the notice of a change of beneficial ownership is lodged; failing to pay it then is a tax default under the Taxation Administration Act 1997 (not deposited)")
